# Derived by hand from Semantics Appendix B (`@PerKey`, round 9 PK: the outer fires only when a key comes or goes, each inner only when its value changes by `==`), ch. 4 (keys are identity: a key that leaves and comes back gets a new row; a newborn row hears nothing of the tick it was born in), ch. 7 (R5: at most once a tick; R7: built at the end of the tick; R8: a key that leaves ends its row at the end of that tick).
test fires_per_key

